
Usage: /WIN <OPEN|CLOSE>
  MTalk  supports text windows.  /WIN OPEN opens two windows.  The top
  one  is where all the output goes, while the bottom one is where you
  type.   You  can  type  at  the same time as messages are displayed.
  /WIN  CLOSE  returns  you  to command line mode.  There are numerous
  control  codes,  that will help you edit your command/message before
  you send it.  These codes are:

  Key       Action
  ---       --------------------------------------
  ^A        Move cursor to beginning of buffer
  <BS>      Delete character to the left of cursor
  ^L        Redraw screen
  <CR>/<LF> Process buffer
  ^X        Delete buffer
  ^K        Delete to the end of buffer
  ^Z        Move cursor to end of buffer
  ^[[A      Move cursor up one line
  ^[[B      Move cursor down one line
  ^[[C      Move cursor one position right
  ^[[D      Move cursor one position left
  <DEL>     Delete character under cursor

  note:
  ^x = hold down the CTRL key and ty/pe <x>
  ^[[A..^[[D are generated by the cursor keys on your keyboard

  See Also:
     /TALK

